---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="AffiliateBharat's privacy policy — what data we collect (and don't), cookies, analytics and affiliate links."
  lang="en"
  canonicalPath="/en/privacy/"
>
  <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/en/' }, { label: 'Privacy' }]} />
  <article class="page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Small site, small policy — what's written here is all we collect.</p>
    <p><em>Last updated: 18 October 2026</em></p>

    <h2>What we do NOT collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>This site has <strong>no accounts, logins or signups</strong> — we never ask for your name, email or phone number.</li>
      <li>We don't store any personal data through forms.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Google Analytics</strong> to understand which articles get read.
      It collects anonymous usage statistics (pages visited, device/browser type).
      Google handles this data under its <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.
      If you prefer not to be tracked, enable "Do Not Track" in your browser or install
      Google's <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">opt-out add-on</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Google Analytics sets its own cookies to recognise repeat visits.
      We don't set any advertising or tracking cookies ourselves.
      You can delete or block cookies in your browser settings at any time — the site works fine without them.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate links and third-party sites</h2>
    <p>
      When you click our affiliate link and land on a merchant's site (a hosting company,
      Flipkart/Amazon, etc.), <strong>their privacy policy</strong> applies, not ours.
      We're not responsible for data you share on those sites.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      This site isn't designed for children, and we don't knowingly collect data from
      children under 13 (we don't collect data at all, so the question barely arises).
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy ever changes, the update will be published here with a new date.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy questions:
      <a href="mailto:hello@affiliatebharat.com">hello@affiliatebharat.com</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page { max-width: 760px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 5vw, 2.6rem); margin: 0 0 0.8rem; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.12rem; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .page h2 { margin: 2.2rem 0 0.8rem; font-size: 1.4rem; }
  .page p, .page li { font-size: 1.02rem; }
  .page ul { padding-left: 1.4rem; }
  .page li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
</style>
